# Line endings, pinned rather than inherited.
#
# The repository stores LF. Without this file the working tree's line endings
# depend on whoever edited a file last, and a tool that rewrites a whole file --
# PowerShell's `Get-Content -Raw | Set-Content`, most commonly -- silently
# converts every line. That is not cosmetic here: it turned a 71-line change to
# auth_host.py into a 1378-line diff, which buries the real change and would make
# a future `git blame` useless for the exact commit that fixed a session-loss bug.
#
# It has happened in this repository already, to these files:
#   src/opencsi/auth/auth_host.py, src/opencsi/auth/session.py,
#   src/opencsi/tray/startup.py, src/opencsi/auth/http_oauth.py
#
# `text=auto` normalises on commit and checks out per `eol`, so an editor that
# writes CRLF cannot get it into the history.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch and PowerShell files are genuinely CRLF: cmd.exe and some
# PowerShell hosts misparse LF-only line endings in .bat/.cmd, and a broken
# build script fails in a way that looks like a missing tool.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary. Listed so `text=auto` never tries to normalise them; a PNG or a SQLite
# profile rewritten as text is unrecoverable.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.pyd binary
*.zip binary
*.whl binary
*.sqlite binary
*.db binary
*.pfx binary
